{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"aa669357-231e-4cdb-bb01-942947809ebe","status":"ERROR","response":"Now let me read the tracker and clusters files, and also run preflight checks in parallel:\nGood - on branch `remediation/main`. Now let me read the existing finding files, baseline, and run preflight checks:\nGood. Now let me read the baseline files and run the preflight checks in parallel:\nGood. Now let me run the current test suite and check if there's a check-tracker script, and also read relevant source files:\nF-011 is already FIXED - `getFinancialYear` already uses IST via `Intl.DateTimeFormat`. Let me check the existing state more carefully and read the other key source files:\nGood. There are immutability triggers already in a migration. Let me read the rejected migration to understand the exact failures and check the current schema:\nThe test suite passed: **22 test files, 103 tests all passed**. This is better than the baseline (20 files, 95 tests). There are already some test files for F-009 and F-011. Let me check what's currently in those test files and read the existing migration:\nI can see the migration uses `OLD.\"salesInvoiceId\"` but the REJECTION note says the correct column name is `\"invoiceId\"`. Let me verify this in the schema and check the existing test results more carefully:\nThe `sales_invoice_line` table has column `invoiceId` (not `salesInvoiceId`). The migration file at line 82 uses `OLD.\"salesInvoiceId\"` which is the **bug**. \n\nNow I have a clear picture. Let me assess what state each finding is in:\n\n**F-009**: REJECTED. The migration has a bug at line 82 - uses `OLD.\"salesInvoiceId\"` but the actual column is `\"invoiceId\"`. Also missing: status downgrade protection, snapshot field protection. The tests in `db-immutability.test.ts` are currently passing (4 tests) but those tests don't test `sales_invoice_line` mutation. \n\n**F-011**: Already FIXED (IST-aware `getFinancialYear` and test both exist and pass).\n\n**F-013**: OPEN - needs `BOUNCED` status in PaymentStatus enum + `bouncePayment()` method + `DebitNote` model.\n\n**F-014**: OPEN - needs TaxRate lookup in sales/finance service.\n\n**F-016**: OPEN - needs `unitConversion` lookup + persistent `warnings` field on `ProductionRun`.\n\nLet me start the fixes one by one. First let me get more context on what I need:\nNow I have a comprehensive understanding of all five findings. Let me plan the work and execute it systematically. I'll use a swarm to handle these in parallel since they're largely independent fixes:\nNow I have full context. Let me execute all the fixes. This is a large task with multiple findings. I'll use the swarm approach to work in parallel on the independent findings. Let me first assess which are truly independent:\n\n- **F-009**: Fix the `sales_invoice_line` trigger bug (column `invoiceId` not `salesInvoiceId`), add status downgrade \u0026 snapshot protection, add `sales_invoice_line` tests  \n- **F-011**: Already FIXED - just need to verify and update tracker  \n- **F-013**: Schema change (add `BOUNCED` to `PaymentStatus`, add `DebitNote` model) + `bouncePayment()` method + tests  \n- **F-014**: Logic change in `sales.service.ts` to look up `TaxRate` by HSN + effective date, with fallback  \n- **F-016**: Schema change (add `packagingWarnings` JSON column to `production_run`) + fix hardcoded logic + tests\n\nF-013 and F-016 require schema migrations. F-009 requires fixing the existing migration. These are schema-independent of each other. Let me proceed with the fix procedure:\nNow I have all the information I need. This is a large fix task. I'll launch the work via a swarm of agents to handle the independent findings in parallel, then I'll handle the sequential parts:\n\nGiven the complexity and interdependence (F-013 schema, F-016 schema must both be done before `prisma migrate dev` and re-generate), let me handle this myself sequentially but efficiently. The order is:\n\n1. **F-009**: Fix `sales_invoice_line` trigger bug + add status downgrade + snapshot protection + tests → commit\n2. **F-011**: Already fixed → verify test passes → update tracker  \n3. **F-013**: Schema (BOUNCED enum + DebitNote model) + migration + bouncePayment() + route + tests → commit\n4. **F-014**: TaxRate lookup in sales.service.ts + tests → commit\n5. **F-016**: Schema (packagingWarnings column) + migration + production.service.ts fix + tests → commit\n\nLet me start with F-009 (fix the trigger bug) and F-011 verification simultaneously:\n\n## F-009: Fix trigger bug + add missing test coverage\n\n**Root cause confirmed**: Migration line 82 uses `COALESCE(OLD.\"salesInvoiceId\", NEW.\"salesInvoiceId\")` but the actual DB column is `\"invoiceId\"`. Also missing: status downgrade protection + snapshot field protection + `sales_invoice_line` tests.\nBug confirmed in DB. The migration SQL needs to be fixed. The existing migration already ran (and is in `_prisma_migrations`), so we need to both:\n1. Fix the migration file for reproducibility on fresh DBs  \n2. Apply the fix to the live DB\n\nLet me write the regression test FIRST (step D), then fix the migration:\nThe DB demonstration failed on schema mismatch (not relevant). The bug is confirmed via pg_proc analysis. Now let me write the before-evidence, then write the regression tests FIRST (they should fail on current broken trigger):\nNow let me write the regression test FIRST (step D) - it should fail on the current buggy code:\nNow let me add the new tests for `sales_invoice_line` and status downgrade to the test file (append the new tests):\nNow run the tests to show them FAILING on the current broken trigger (step D - regression test failing before fix):\nThe tests are FAILING as expected on the current buggy code. 2 new tests fail:\n1. \"rejects mutation of snapshot fields\" - trigger doesn't block `companyGstinSnapshot` updates\n2. Need to check which one else failed...\n\nLet me run again to see both failures clearly:\nThe failing tests confirm the bugs:\n- **Status downgrade** (`POSTED → DRAFT`) is not blocked - `UPDATE 1` succeeds\n- **Snapshot fields** (`companyGstinSnapshot`) are not blocked - `UPDATE 1` succeeds\n- **sales_invoice_line trigger** is working (was fixed when beforeAll re-runs the migration SQL each time... but the existing trigger has the bug) - Wait, the line tests are PASSING with `42703` error... that means the test IS passing because the trigger throws an error (even though it's the wrong error), which counts as a rejection. Let me check: yes, `42703` is a \"field not found\" error which causes the trigger to crash, which the test sees as a rejection. So those tests PASS for the wrong reason!\n\nThis is important - the line trigger tests pass because the broken trigger crashes with a different error (column not found). But the actual fix is still needed because:\n1. It crashes with an internal error rather than the proper immutability message\n2. Any legitimate UPDATE/DELETE on a DRAFT invoice line would also crash\n\nNow let me implement the fix. I'll update the migration SQL file AND apply the fix to the live DB:\nNow apply the fixed migration to the live DB (the test's `beforeAll` re-applies it, but let's also apply directly):\n**All 8 immutability tests pass.** Now let me commit F-009 and proceed to the other findings:\nF-009 committed. Now let me handle F-011 (verify it's already fixed) and proceed to F-013, F-014, F-016 in parallel:\n\n**F-011**: Already verified - `getFinancialYear` uses IST, `financial-year-tz.test.ts` has 4 passing tests. Just need to update tracker.\n\nNow let me tackle **F-013** (payment bounce + DebitNote) simultaneously with **F-016** (packaging warnings schema):\nNow I have full understanding. Let me implement F-013. The plan:\n1. Add `BOUNCED` to `PaymentStatus` enum in schema\n2. Add `DebitNote` model in schema  \n3. Create migration for schema changes\n4. Add `bouncePayment()` to `payment.service.ts`\n5. Add bounce route to `payment.routes.ts`\n6. Add regression test\n\nLet me write the regression test FIRST:\nGood - confirmed `bouncePayment` doesn't exist. Now write the failing test:\nNow let me also check how existing tests set up orders - I need to have approved orders in the test. Let me look at the payments test for context:\nThe existing tests use HTTP - they're higher level. For my bounce test I'll use service-layer directly. But I need approved orders. Let me simplify the test to build data from scratch:\nTests fail as expected - `bouncePayment is not a function` and `BOUNCED` enum value missing. Now let me implement the fix.\n\n## Step E: Implement F-013 fix\n\n**Schema changes needed:**\n1. Add `BOUNCED` to `PaymentStatus` enum\n2. Add `DebitNote` model (as per OD-06 decision)\n\n**Service changes:**\n1. Add `bouncePayment(paymentId, reason)` to `PaymentService`\n\n**Route changes:**\n1. Add `POST /api/v1/payments/:id/bounce`\nNow add the `DebitNote` model and add `debitNotes` relation to Payment. First, let me find where to add DebitNote (after PaymentAllocation):\nI accidentally mangled the AuditLog. Let me fix it and add the DebitNote model in the right place:\nThe AuditLog model is missing its `id` field. Let me fix that:\nAlso need to add `debitNotes` relation to Organization. Let me check if Organization has a relation list:\nNeed to add `debitNotes` relation to Organization model:\nNow also need to fix the DebitNote model - the `organizationId` and `organization` fields look like they're in the wrong order. Let me view:\n","error":"Individual quota reached. Please upgrade your subscription to increase your limits. Resets in 62h50m46s.","duration_seconds":496.655755663,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":145237,"output_tokens":24852,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":5383366,"total_tokens":170089},"finished_reason":"error"}}
